Warrick,<br />
<br />
You asked whether the October search could have missed the document. We hav=
e now closed the two openings you identified and the answer is no.<br />
<br />
First, we widened and re-ran. The mailbox list was extended to the regional=
 director's office and to the two examiners who joined the branch in 2013, =
the date range was extended through December 31, 2014, and the term list wa=
s extended to the registrant's outside counsel's domain and to the names of=
 the two accounting firms the registrant used. That is 7,940 messages in sc=
ope. Eleven additional matches, all of them 2014 correspondence about the f=
irm's annual amendment. Nothing responsive to Count II.<br />
<br />
Second, Percival raised the EXAMTRAC restore, which returned this morning. =
The retired platform holds the complete 2012-0331 work paper set - 214 docu=
ments, including the examiner's fieldwork notes, the sampling worksheets, t=
he exit interview memorandum and the closing recommendation. The closing re=
commendation is one page and reads that no deficiencies were identified and=
 that the examination should be closed C-1. There is no draft deficiency le=
tter and no undertaking in the work papers either.<br />
<br />
So we have two independent systems, one of which is the case system's own r=
etired predecessor and the other of which is the message archive that has n=
ever lost anything since 2004, and they agree. The undertaking pleaded in C=
ount II was not lost in the migration. It was never created.<br />
<br />
Han-Wei Loh